OL,3,GNEWSAMan jailed for mosque threats
OL,4,Aafter synagogue attack
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man who made death threats to two
OL,7,Fmosques in the wake of the Manchester
OL,8,Fsynagogue attack has been jailed for
OL,9,Fmore than two years.
OL,11,FGabriel Levy, 21, from Wakefield, made
OL,12,Fan anonymous phone call to the
OL,13,FAl-Sunnah Mosque in Cheetham Hill on 4
OL,14,FOctober 2025, telling the person who
OL,15,Fanswered: "I'm going to come to your
OL,16,Fmosque and kill you," according to the
OL,17,FCrown Prosecution Service (CPS).
OL,19,FWhen Levy, who is Jewish, was arrested
OL,20,Fhe told police he did it in response to
OL,21,Fthe attack two days earlier, in which
OL,22,Ftwo men were killed.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
